    "text": "At Aethel Facility, shift supervisors must lock bay `B-42` when radiation exceeds 15 mSv/h. When radiation is below 15 mSv/h, the shift supervisor may unlock `B-42` only if authorization `AUTH-992` is valid. Even with valid authorization, the supervisor is not obligated to unlock the bay. If secondary sensors show anomalies, the supervisor should request a sweep before unlocking. Maintenance technicians can monitor radiation levels on the dashboard, but they must not authorize `AUTH-992` or unlock the bay.",
